#
# holt — Nim for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Nim symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Nim`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Nim parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Nim\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Nim ########################################################################
--langdef=HoltNim
--map-HoltNim=+.nim
--map-HoltNim=+.nims
--kinddef-HoltNim=f,function,procs
--kinddef-HoltNim=c,class,types
--kinddef-HoltNim=v,variable,variables
--regex-HoltNim=/^[ \t]*(proc|func|method|iterator|template|macro|converter)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\2/f/
--regex-HoltNim=/^[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)\*?[ \t]*=[ \t]*(ref[ \t]+)?(object|enum|tuple|distinct)/\1/c/
--regex-HoltNim=/^[ \t]*(var|let|const)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\2/v/
